5. Deep-Dive into the Tenuto 6.0 Synthesis & Physical Modeling Engines (TDB-716–TDB-725)
To ensure that every patch="..." in Tenuto 6.0 delivers studio-grade sound without relying on external proprietary plugins, Phase 4 and Phase 5 implement dedicated DSP engines for Ableton's complete instrument roster alongside our 128-instrument MusyngKite HD SoundFont streaming library (SoundfontLibrary.ts).
5.1 Wavetable (WavetableEngine.ts — TDB-716)
When a track declares style=synth patch="wavetable", Tenuto instantiates a dual-oscillator morphing wavetable voice with:
Continuous Frame Interpolation: Each oscillator holds a 2D wavetable matrix W[m][k] of M frames by K=2048 samples. Given a normalized wave_pos parameter [0,1] (modulatable via .cc(), LFO, or MPE Slide), the engine interpolates adjacent band-limited frames in real time:  s_{\text{osc}}(t) = (1 - \beta),W_{\lfloor \alpha(M-1) \rfloor}(\phi(t)) + \beta,W_{\lceil \alpha(M-1) \rceil}(\phi(t)), \quad \beta = \alpha(M-1) - \lfloor \alpha(M-1) \rfloor 
Unison Modes: Supports up to 8-voice stereo unison per oscillator across Classic, Shimmer (jittered pitch intervals), Noise, and Phase Sync topologies.
Modulation Matrix: 3 ADSR envelopes and 2 tempo-synced LFOs mapped via macros=@{...} or env=@{...} dictionaries.
5.2 Operator 4-Op FM & Additive Synth (OperatorEngine.ts — TDB-717)
For patch="operator", Tenuto constructs a 4-operator frequency-modulation graph (A,B,C,D) supporting all 11 classic Ableton Operator routing topologies (from pure serial cascade DCBA to 4-carrier additive parallel A+B+C+D):
$$
y_A(t) = A_{\text{env}}(t) \sin\!\Big(2\pi f_0 r_A t + I_B(t) \sin\big(2\pi f_0 r_B t + I_C(t)\sin(2\pi f_0 r_C t)\big)\Big)
$$

where rA,rB,rC,rD are the coarse/fine harmonic ratios (ratioA, ratioB, etc.) and Ik(t) are the time-variant modulation indices governed by each operator's envelope.
5.3 Meld Bi-Timbral Macro-Oscillator (MeldEngine.ts — TDB-718)
Introduced in Ableton Live 12, Meld pairs two macro-oscillator engines (A and B) that are explicitly aware of the project's scale (meta @{ key: "D", scale: "harmonic_minor" }). When a producer selects Meld's Swarm, Chord, or Harmonic oscillator modes, pitch detuning and partial quantization automatically snap to the active scale degrees so polyphonic textures never clash harmonically.
5.4 Physical Modeling (Collision, Tension, Electric — TDB-720) & Granular (Granulator III — TDB-724)
Collision & Tension: Uses tuned 2-pole modal resonator banks and Karplus-Strong waveguide delay lines (L=fsf0) with nonlinear bow/mallet excitation models to synthesize realistic marimbas, vibraphones, membranes, and bowed/plucked strings.
Granulator III: Slices any src="..." audio buffer (or live audio input) into overlapping raised-cosine grains of length $d_g \in [2\text{ ms}, 500\text{ ms}]$ with controllable spray, scan, and per-grain pitch jitter.
5.5 128-Pad Drum Rack with Choke Groups & Per-Pad FX (TDB-723)
Upgrading style=grid, Tenuto 6.0's Drum Rack allows every trigger token (k, s, cp, h, oh, lt, mt, ht, cr, rd, or any MIDI note $0\dots 127$) to host its own Drum Sampler instance, independent per-pad .fx() chain, and Choke Group assignment (1–16). When a closed hi-hat (h, Choke Group 1) triggers while an open hi-hat (oh, Choke Group 1) is ringing, the engine executes a $6\text{ ms}$ de-clicked choke fade on oh, matching hardware MPC and Ableton Drum Rack behavior.

