6.1 Audio Effects Highlights
EQ Eight (TDB-727): Up to 8 biquad filter stages per channel (Stereo, Left/Right, or Mid/Side matrix encoding $M = \frac{L+R}{\sqrt{2}}, \; S = \frac{L-R}{\sqrt{2}}$) overlaid on a real-time 60 FPS AnalyserNode FFT spectrum canvas. Dragging a filter node on the spectrum canvas updates .fx(eq_eight, @{bell1_freq: 950, bell1_db: -3.5, bell1_q: 1.4}) in the .ten editor on mouse release.
Roar Multi-Stage Saturator (TDB-730): Splits incoming audio into Low, Mid, and High crossover bands (or serial/parallel stages), applies polynomial/tanh waveshaping curves with a frequency-dispersive feedback loop, and locks its feedback filter to the incoming MIDI pitch.
Hybrid Reverb (TDB-731): Combines our stereo Concertgebouw/Studio convolution engine with five algorithmic decay networks (Shimmer with $+12\text{ st}$ pitch-shifted feedback, Dark, Quartz, Tides, and Prism).
Auto Shift & Spectral Resonator (TDB-733, TDB-734): Performs real-time autocorrelation pitch detection and phase-locked pitch/formant shifting quantized to the score's meta @{ key, scale }.
6.2 Live 12 MIDI Transformations, Generators & MPE (TDB-736–TDB-740)
Because Tenuto's Piano Roll is a direct projection of .ten code, Ableton Live 12's MIDI Transformations (Arpeggiate, Connect, Ornament, Accelerate/Decelerate, Strum, Span) and MIDI Generators (Rhythm, Seed, Shape, Stacks) operate as AST Code Generators. Selecting 2 bars on the Piano Roll and clicking Generate: Stacks writes scale-locked chord voicings directly into the .ten measure block, where they can be immediately edited by hand or by an AI copilot.
Furthermore, per-note MPE (MIDI Polyphonic Expression) modifiers (.mpe(@{bend: [0, 12, 0], slide: [30, 110], pressure: [70, 120]})) allocate an independent synthesis voice and filter per note within a chord so that one note in a triad can bend up an octave while the other two notes remain stationary.

7. Elastic Audio Warping, Comping & AI Stem Separation (TDB-741–TDB-745)
To bring recorded vocals, guitars, and sample loops (style=concrete and style=simpler) to full parity with Ableton's audio engine, Phase 9 upgrades TenutoProcessor.ts (AudioWorklet) with elastic time-stretching and pitch-shifting:
Five Elastic Warp Modes (TDB-741):
warp(beats): Detects transient onsets and preserves percussive attacks while time-stretching decay tails to match meta @{ tempo }.
warp(tones) & warp(texture): Pitch-synchronous overlap-add (PSOLA) and granular cloud stretching for monophonic melodies and ambient pads.
warp(repitch): Classic variable-speed tape resampling where playback rate scales proportionally with tempo ($\text{rate} = \frac{\text{BPM}_{\text{target}}}{\text{BPM}_{\text{source}}}$).
warp(complex) & warp(complex_pro): Short-Time Fourier Transform (STFT) phase-vocoder time-stretching with spectral envelope formant preservation (.formant(15%)), allowing a full stereo mix or vocal phrase to be transposed (transpose(-3st)) or stretched across wide tempo changes without "chipmunk" formant artifacts.
Multi-Pass Audio Recording & Take Lane Comping (TDB-742): Recording audio while looping a 4-bar section stacks each pass into numbered Take Lanes (take 1, take 2, take 3) inside the .ten track block. Highlighting segments across takes in the UI compiles a seamless master comp with automatic $10\text{ ms}$ equal-power crossfades.
Built-In AI Stem Separation & Audio-to-.ten Decompilation (TDB-743, TDB-744): Right-clicking any audio clip provides two transformative actions:
Separate Stems: Splits a mixed audio file into four isolated .ten tracks (def vox_stem, def drums_stem, def bass_stem, def other_stem).
Convert Audio to .ten (Harmony / Melody / Drums): Runs polyphonic pitch/onset transcription on an audio recording and writes the resulting chords, melodies, or drum triggers directly into clean, idiomatic .ten code.

8. Why Code-Driven Ableton Parity Changes Everything
By uniting 100% of Ableton Live 12 Suite's instrument, effect, session, and audio-warping capabilities with Tenuto 6.0's declarative .ten compiler, Tenuto Studio 6.0 unlocks workflows that no binary DAW can replicate:
True Version Control ("Git for the Entire Studio"): Every change to a mix—whether adding a +2.5 dB high-shelf on eq_eight, changing a clip's Follow Action probability from 75% to 90%, or transposing a Meld pad—is a clean, readable 1-line diff in Git. Producers can branch arrangements, open pull requests on remixes, and revert a single synth macro change from three weeks ago without losing newer vocal takes.
Zero-Hallucination Human-AI Co-Production: Instead of generating uneditable black-box MP3s, an AI agent (Gemini, Claude, or the built-in LanceDB Copilot) has full, deterministic control over every knob, synth oscillator, drum pad, send level, and automation curve in the DAW. You can ask an AI to "Duck the synth_bus by 4 dB against drums, add a dotted-eighth ping-pong echo send on lead in Scene 2, and humanize the hi-hat velocities between 65 and 105," and watch both the .ten source code and the visual DAW update in real time.
Instant Portability & Archival Permanence: A complete multi-scene, 16-track Tenuto 6.0 production fits in a $35\text{ KB}$ .ten text file (or a self-contained .tenpack archive when bundled with custom vocal recordings) and renders bit-identically in a web browser or native macOS .pkg desktop app—today or twenty years from now.
